# Required for the web build to work at all.
#
# expo-sqlite runs SQLite in the browser through wa-sqlite, and its worker
# channel allocates a SharedArrayBuffer. Browsers only expose SharedArrayBuffer
# to CROSS-ORIGIN ISOLATED pages, which means the server must send both headers
# below. Served without them, the database layer throws on startup — the build
# succeeding tells you nothing about this.
#
# This file is the Netlify / Cloudflare Pages format and is copied into dist/ by
# `expo export`. Other hosts need the same two headers configured their own way;
# `npx serve` and `python -m http.server` do NOT send them, so local testing of
# persistence needs a server that does.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
